-- title:
--   Mass of a conjugated maximal order at a finite place
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $[L:K]=2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the cyclic group generated by $\sigma$, let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ and $u$ an idele unit, where $\mathbf{A}_K$ is the adele ring of $\mathcal{O}_K$. Write $\delta$ for the product of the image of $\delta_0$ under $L \to L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ with the scalar matrix of $c$. Assume (hN) that the norm string of $\delta$, namely the product $\prod_{i<[L:K]} (\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}})^{i}(\delta)$, equals the image of the central scalar matrix of $u$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K)$, and (hns) that there are no $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $z \in L^\times$ with $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x)$ a scalar matrix $z$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and let $\delta_v$ be the image of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Let $\tau$ be a Haar measure on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $T'_v$ of $\delta_v$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ (with its Borel structure), let $t_v \in [0,\infty]$, and let $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be such that the image of the $v$-component of the central scalar matrix of $u$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ equals $y^{-1} \cdot (\text{norm string of } \delta_v) \cdot y$, and such that (hmap) the pushforward of $\tau$ along $t \mapsto y^{-1} t y$ equals $t_v$ times the pushforward of the local Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ along $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. Let $S_M$ be an additive subgroup of $M_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ equal to the additive closure of the set of matrices $y\,(1 \otimes g)\,y^{-1}$ with $g \in M_2(K_v)$ having all entries in the valuation ring of $K_v$. Then, with $q_v = \mathrm{absNorm}(v)$,
--   $$\int^{-}_{\{t \in T'_v \,:\, t \in S_M\}} \bigl\| N_{(L \otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t) \bigr\| \, d\tau(t) = t_v \cdot (1 - q_v^{-2})^{-1}\,(1 - q_v^{1-2})^{-1},$$
--   the integrand being the $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^\infty$-valued function given by the absolute value of the $K_v$-algebra norm of the determinant.
--
--   This is the local mass computation for the reference order $y\,(1 \otimes M_2(\mathcal{O}_v))\,y^{-1}$: the additive measure $\|N\det\| \cdot \tau$ of the twisted centraliser assigns it the value $t_v \zeta_v(2)\zeta_v(1)$, obtained from the local twisted orbital zeta integral at $s = 2$ with the characteristic function of the order. It feeds the finite-covolume estimate [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar).
